A move gives the destination its budget and leaves the source's as it was.
Every move then makes processor time out of nothing;
the budgets of the shares add up to the whole processor.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: the budgets of the shares do not add up to the whole processor

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -575,7 +575,6 @@ static int op_share(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
         /* What one share gives the other takes, so the budgets still add up to the whole. */
-        from->budget -= arg[3];
         to->budget += arg[3];
         sched_share_changed(from);
         sched_share_changed(to);
